<section class="lp-section lp-audiences" id="for-whom" aria-labelledby="lp-audiences-title" data-testid="landing-for-whom">
    <div class="lp-container">
        <div class="lp-split-head">
            <div>
                <p class="lp-eyebrow">Who it is for</p>
                <h2 class="lp-h2" id="lp-audiences-title">For anyone who has to put something in writing.</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="lp-lede">You need no technical knowledge and no special way of asking. Pick where you are; each link leads to the part of the explanation that fits.</p>
        </div>

        <ul class="aud-list">
            <li class="aud" data-testid="landing-for-whom-home">
                <h3>At home</h3>
                <p>A letter to the landlord, the insurance or an office. A note for the neighbours. An email you have put off for a week.</p>
                <a href="/how-it-works#steps" data-enhance-nav="false">The steps</a>
            </li>
            <li class="aud" data-testid="landing-for-whom-clubs">
                <h3>Clubs and schools</h3>
                <p>An invitation, a letter to parents, a short report from your notes or the minutes of a meeting.</p>
                <a href="/how-it-works#example" data-enhance-nav="false">An example</a>
            </li>
            <li class="aud" data-testid="landing-for-whom-office">
                <h3>Self-employed and small offices</h3>
                <p>Emails to customers, a summary of a long document, a text written from your own files. Under About me you say once who you are, so you need not repeat it.</p>
                <a href="/how-it-works#files" data-enhance-nav="false">Your files</a>
            </li>
            <li class="aud" data-testid="landing-for-whom-assistant">
                <h3>People who use an AI assistant</h3>
                <p>Connect Atelier to your assistant through MCP (tested with Claude Code). Atelier asks the assistant to pass on your words unchanged and to ask you its questions. The full result is always in the web app too.</p>
                <a href="/how-it-works#assistant" data-enhance-nav="false">From an AI assistant</a>
            </li>
            <li class="aud" data-testid="landing-for-whom-admins">
                <h3>Administrators and developers</h3>
                <p>Add people, decide which features are on, and host it yourself: Atelier is open source.</p>
                <a href="/how-it-works#admins" data-enhance-nav="false">For administrators</a>
                <a href="/how-it-works#developers" data-enhance-nav="false">For developers and hosts</a>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</section>
